{
  "about": "Implant upgrade trees (engine/upgrades.ts). Every implant grows its own tree, worked out from the implant itself (always the same for the same part): its rarity sets the size and depth (shapes), its maker which upgrades turn up (each kind lists the makers that lean on it; 'any' suits every maker). Inner nodes come from kinds, the end of every branch is a capstone, and only a legendary implant ends its deepest branch in a legendary capstone. Numbers grow with rarity (scale) and capstones with how deep they sit. A node needs its parent; the children of one node are a fork. costs[d] is the price of a node d steps from the root. effect: dmg (share of damage), heat (added to the move's heat), steady (aim one step steadier), precise (always full damage), guard (share of guard), attack/defense/hp/move/evasion (stats), fx (side effects, as on implant parts).",
